  "non_claims": [
    "Not an R1000 closure artifact and not a semantic or legal interpretation; R1000 stays active/unclosed.",
    "The counts document is a counts-only read of the materialized JSONL layers; it is NOT an independent substrate verification and NOT an authenticity claim.",
    "A partial run is never reported as full (partial_is_not_full=true).",
    "No raw decoded text reaches receipts, the report, diagnostics or stdout; every persisted string is a path, a hash, a count or a closed token.",
    "The S03 baseline is an acceptance/integrity baseline, not a semantic oracle; S07 reconciles counts only.",
    "The proof subset is a deterministic sample of the pinned manifest; its receipt bindings are snapshot-bound and shift with any tracked-file change.",
    "The SIGTERM interruption is enforced by a real signal to the harness process; the harness signal handler unwinds the live-poll loop, which SIGKILLs and reaps the in-flight consumer child, so an interrupted attempt never orphans a consumer.",
    "Whether the pinned corpus emits any typed consumer refusal is a result of the run, reported by the ledger's refused_by_class, and is never asserted in advance."
  ],
  "note": "the consumer imports the same materialized JSONL layers twice; the repeat import is an idempotent no-op and the counts are byte-identical",
